  "discussion": {
    "headline": "big cooldown this weekend with first widespread frosts of season",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Friday, October 16, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "Following a partly sunny and pleasant Thursday with high temperatures in the mid-to-upper 60s, south-southwesterly winds of 10-20 mph will usher unseasonably warm and humid air back into the Lower Susquehanna Valley this afternoon. There should at least be a few hours of sunshine prior to the arrival of a line of heavy, gusty showers, and high temperatures should reach the mid 70s to low 80s from east-to-west across the region with dewpoints in the mid-to-upper 60s (see below …",
